ss":"obtain"},{"text":"இசின்","lemma":"இசின்","gloss":"expletive"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"obtained indeed"}]}],"literal":"Fine-haired plump forearms / bright-jeweled innocent women / for the doll made of streaked sand / plucking flowers from curved branches / plunge into the cool waters of Porunai / in victorious Vañci of sky-reaching fame / the victorious king worthy of songs / conquered the strongholds of fierce heat / and saw the backs of his enemies. / The victorious king who saw their backs, / the songstress who sang of his valor / obtained beautiful, excellent gold coins / and fine ornaments. / To the songstress who obtained ornaments, / the male bard skilled in singing tunes matching her voice / in that manner / a lotus made of bright fire / obtained as a flower on a silver string.","translation":"In victorious Vañci, whose sky-reaching fame is worthy of songs, innocent women with bright jewels and fine-haired, plump forearms pluck flowers from curved branches to offer to their dolls made of streaked sand, and plunge into the cool waters of the Porunai river. Its victorious king conquered the fierce strongholds of his enemies and saw their backs in defeat. The songstress who sang of the valor of this victorious king who saw their backs obtained beautiful, excellent gold coins and fine ornaments. And the male bard, skilled in singing tunes that match her voice, in that very manner, obtained a lotus of bright fire, strung on a silver thread.","modern":"வானை முட்டும் புகழுடைய, பாடல்களில் போற்றப்படும் வஞ்சி மாநகரிலே, மெல்லிய முடிகளையும் திரண்ட முன் கைகளையும் உடைய, விளங்கும் அணிகலன்களை அணிந்த இளம்பெண்கள், வரியமைந்த மணலால் செய்த பாவைக்காக வளைந்த கிளைகளிலிருந்து பூக்களைக் கொய்து, குளிர்ந்த பொருநை ஆற்றின் நீரில் குதித்து விளையாடுவர். அத்தகைய வஞ்சி நகரின் வெற்றிவேந்தன், பகைவர்களின் வெம்மை பொருந்திய கோட்டைகளை வென்று அவர்களின் முதுகைக் கண்டான் (தோற்கடித்தான்). அவ்வாறு பகைவரை வென்ற வெற்றிவேந்தனின் வீரத்தைப் பாடிய பாடினி, அழகிய சிறந்த பொற்காசுகளையும் சிறந்த அணிகலன்களையும் பரிசாகப் பெற்றாள். அவ்வாறு அணிகலன்களைப் பெற்ற பாடினியோடு குரல் சேர்த்துப் பாடும் திறமைமிக்க பாணனும், ஒளிவீசும் நெருப்புப் போன்ற பொற்றாமரைப் பூவை வெள்ளி நாரில் தொடுத்துப் பரிசாகப் பெற்றான்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the paṭāṇ tiṇai and the theme is paricil kaṭānilai (soliciting gifts), composed by the poetess Pēymakaḷ Iḷaveyiṉiyār in praise of the Cēra king Pālai Pāṭiya Peruṅkaṭuṅkō. The poetess describes the prosperity and beauty of the Cēra capital, Vañci, where young women play with sand dolls and bathe in the cool Porunai river, contrasting this peaceful domestic scene with the king's fierce military victories. The king has defeated his enemies, conquering their hot, formidable fortresses. In celebration of his valor, the female singer (pāṭiṉi) is rewarded with heavy gold coins and fine jewelry. Consequently, her companion, the male bard (pāṇaṉ), who harmonizes with her voice, is presented with a golden lotus flower (resembling bright fire) strung on a silver thread. Through these vivid descriptions of artistic rewards, the poetess subtly prompts the king for her own well-deserved gifts.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.7],[0.7,1.0],[1.0,1.5],[1.5,1.8],[1.8,2.1],[2.1,2.3],[2.3,3.12],[3.12,3.45],[3.45,3.8],[3.8,4.14],[4.14,5.62],[5.62,5.79],[5.79,6.06],[6.06,6.25],[6.25,6.52],[6.52,6.7],[6.7,7.2],[7.2,7.5],[7.5,8.1],[8.1,8.5],[8.5,8.99],[9.05,9.8],[9.8,10.6],[10.6,11.0],[11.0,11.41],[11.41,11.8],[11.8,12.3],[12.3,12.5],[12.5,12.7],[12.7,13.3],[13.96,14.52],[14.52,14.98],[14.98,15.26],[15.26,15.54],[15.54,15.81],[15.81,16.0],[16.0,16.16],[16.16,17.66],[17.66,17.86],[17.86,18.06],[18.06,18.46],[18.46,18.83],[19.01,19.56],[19.56,19.76],[19.76,20.12],[20.26,21.36],[21.36,21.76],[21.76,22.09],[22.09,22.91],[23.14,23.36],[23.36,23.56],[23.56,24.01],[24.01,24.46],[24.46,25.16],[25.16,25.56],[25.56,26.46],[26.46,27.06],[27.06,27.36],[27.36,27.76],[28.48,29.18],[29.18,29.48],[29.48,29.78],[29.78,30.7